cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SHIR in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SHIR: System for Hybrid Image Reconstruction"
abstract: >-
  An open-source desktop application that reconstructs raw MRI data (Siemens
  TWIX .dat, from product and Pulseq sequences) into images, quality metrics,
  PDF reports and NumPy arrays without programming. It reads k-space line
  positions from the TWIX header or the played Pulseq .seq file, runs the same
  pipelines on BART or SigPy with shared parameters, and simulates
  undersampling of existing fully sampled scans.
